## Automated AI review

> **Community review:** Independent automated community review, unaffiliated with the Omarchy team, intended to help prepare PRs for their review.

**Outcome:** Two live updates leave stale group layout; open PR #13139 reuses `group`.

### Anchor keeps a stale group

`applySettingsDelta` overwrites the `slot.group` binding; the anchor slot survives rebuilds. After `omarchy bar set omarchy.clock group X`, a rebuild dropping the group (such as `omarchy bar defaults` after a reorder) keeps the clock in X.

**Suggested change:** restore the binding in `onEntryChanged`.

<details><summary>Reproducer (fails at 5c7cccbf; a QML model built from Bar.qml lines)</summary>

# Center anchor keeps a stale group after a live group change

Reproduces the anchor slot keeping the group set by applySettingsDelta after a later layout rebuild hands it an entry without a group. The anchor slot (centerAnchorModule) is not inside a Repeater, so it is the one slot object that survives rebuilds.

Reviewed head: 5c7cccbfe0fbe5f1bb3e731ffe87be00bf399f52. Qt 6.11.2, offscreen platform.

Run from a scratch directory holding this file and a copy of `shell/plugins/bar/BarModel.js` from the PR head:

```bash
QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen /usr/lib/qt6/bin/qmltestrunner -input tst_anchor_group_stale.qml
```

`tst_anchor_group_stale.qml`:

```qml
// Stale group on the center anchor after a live `omarchy bar set <anchor> group ...`.
// Lines tagged "Bar.qml:N" are copied from shell/plugins/bar/Bar.qml at 5c7cccbf.
// Run from a directory holding this file and shell/plugins/bar/BarModel.js:
//   QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen /usr/lib/qt6/bin/qmltestrunner -input tst_anchor_group_stale.qml
import QtQuick
import QtTest
import "BarModel.js" as BarModel

Item {
  id: root

  function entrySettings(entry) { return BarModel.entrySettings(entry) }
  function entryId(entry) { return BarModel.entryId(entry) }

  // centerAnchorModule (Bar.qml:1633) is declared directly in the center section,
  // not inside a Repeater, so a layout rebuild re-evaluates its `entry` binding on
  // the same object instead of creating a new slot.
  Item {
    id: anchorSlot
    property var entry: ({ id: "omarchy.clock", format: "dddd HH:mm" })
    property string region: "center"
    readonly property string moduleName: root.entryId(entry)
    readonly property var moduleSettings: root.entrySettings(entry)                  // Bar.qml:2020
    property string group: moduleSettings.group ? String(moduleSettings.group) : ""  // Bar.qml:2024
  }

  // applySettingsDelta's new lines (Bar.qml:612-616), reached by
  // `omarchy bar set omarchy.clock group time` through the inline settings delta.
  function applySettingsDelta(entry) {
    var settings = entrySettings(entry)
    var slot = anchorSlot
    var group = settings.group ? String(settings.group) : ""
    if (slot.group !== group) {
      slot.group = group
    }
  }

  TestCase {
    name: "AnchorGroup"

    function test_anchor_group_follows_its_entry_after_a_rebuild() {
      // 1. omarchy bar set omarchy.clock group time
      applySettingsDelta({ id: "omarchy.clock", format: "dddd HH:mm", group: "time" })
      compare(anchorSlot.group, "time")

      // 2. A later change that rebuilds the layout (for example `omarchy bar defaults`
      //    after any reorder) hands the anchor slot a fresh entry without `group`.
      anchorSlot.entry = { id: "omarchy.clock", format: "dddd HH:mm" }
      compare(anchorSlot.moduleSettings.group, undefined, "the new entry has no group")
      compare(anchorSlot.group, "", "the anchor's group follows the new entry")
    }
  }
}
```

