### Anchor at a group end sits off centre

`anchors.centerIn` centres the padded slot, so an anchor at one end of a group sits `(lead − trail) / 2` off centre (6 px, then 3 px when its neighbour hides), unlike the "dead center" promise in `manual/05-the-top-bar.md`.

**Suggested change:** offset the anchor by `(trailInset − leadInset) / 2` along the bar.

# Anchored widget leaves the exact centre when it sits at a group end

Reproduces the anchor's content shifting by (lead inset - trail inset) / 2 because the padded slot, not the widget, is centred; the shift changes when the neighbour on the other side hides.

