**Optional test improvement:** 7 of 10 deliberate code mutations still pass `bar-test.sh`. The live-regroup regex `/slot\.group = group[\s\S]*?scheduleGroups\(\)/` still matches after the regroup call is deleted, because it runs on to a later `scheduleGroups()`. Limiting it to `applySettingsDelta` would make it guard that call.

# The live-regroup assertion passes without the regroup call

Test-validity reproducer. `test/shell.d/bar-test.sh` asserts `/slot\.group = group[\s\S]*?scheduleGroups\(\)/` for "changing a widget group live regroups its section". The lazy `[\s\S]*?` can run on to any later `scheduleGroups()` in Bar.qml, so the assertion still passes when the call it is meant to guard is removed.

Reviewed head: 5c7cccbfe0fbe5f1bb3e731ffe87be00bf399f52.

